1
00:04:54,000 --> 00:05:00,000
Meet Phillip and Marlowe, the post-nuclear private eyes. They're looking for good
times and fast women. Their first case could be the world's last.

2
00:09:48,000 --> 00:09:54,000
Radioactive Dreams is a science fiction, action,
adventure film directed by Albert Pyun.

3
00:14:42,000 --> 00:14:48,000
After an atomic war Phillip Hammer and Marlowe Chandler have spent 15 years on their own
in an bunker, stuffed with junk from the 40s and old detective novels.

4
00:19:36,000 --> 00:19:42,000
Now, 19 years old, they leave their shelter to find a
world full of mutants, freaks and cannibals.

5
00:24:30,000 --> 00:24:36,000
They become famous detectives in the struggle for the two
keys that could fire the last nuclear weapon.

6
00:29:24,000 --> 00:29:30,000
Phillip Chandler, played by John Stockwell.

7
00:34:18,000 --> 00:34:24,000
Marlowe Hammer, played by Michael Dudikoff.

8
00:39:12,000 --> 00:39:18,000
Miles Archer, played by Lisa Blount.

9
00:44:06,000 --> 00:44:12,000
Spade Chandler, played by George Kennedy.

10
00:49:00,000 --> 00:49:06,000
Dash Hammer, played by Don Murray.

11
00:53:54,000 --> 00:54:00,000
Rusty Mars, played by Michele Little.

12
00:58:48,000 --> 00:58:54,000
Radioactive Dreams is a 1984 post-apocalyptic science fiction-comedy film written and directed by
Albert Pyun and starring George Kennedy, Michael Dudikoff, Don Murray, and Lisa Blount.

13
01:03:42,000 --> 01:03:48,000
The names of the two main characters are homages to noir detective fiction
icons Philip Marlowe, Raymond Chandler and Mike Hammer.

14
01:08:36,000 --> 01:08:42,000
The film has achieved cult status and has been screened in
several cult revival programs around the world.

15
01:13:30,000 --> 01:13:36,000
The film begins with two boys growing up in a fallout
shelter, in an attempt to escape a nuclear war.

16
01:18:24,000 --> 01:18:30,000
They rejoin the world in 2001, and soon acquire the
activation keys of the world's last nuclear missile.

17
01:23:18,000 --> 01:23:24,000
They get involved in gang warfare in their new environment.

18
01:28:12,000 --> 01:28:18,000
The film explores themes of detective, mutant, post-apocalyptic future.

19
01:33:06,000 --> 01:33:12,000
The tone is lighthearted and thought_provoking.
